Subject: [PATCH] Lean statement packet, round 7: Side24 successor interface
 pinning the cone moment (specified)

Appends to Specifications/Side24.lean, after every existing declaration (byte-identical), the
successor interface PeriodicCoefficientInterface2 (every field of PeriodicCoefficientInterface
plus the parent's nondegeneracy clause as pinCov_posDef and condHessianCov_posDef, and
coneMoment_def pinning the given cone moment to the Gaussian cone expectation under
multivariateGaussian 0 (condHessianCov d (K24 d) u R), the Schur complement of the
derivative-rule blocks), the successor Props CoefficientEnclosure2 and ReferenceComparison2
over it, and the nine auxiliary definitions they need. REGISTER.json gains the three statement
rows under side24-coefficient (all `specified`) and one sentence each in that row's
not_established and next_step; README.md and SCOPE.md are re-rendered from the register
(153 registered declarations: 143 Props, 10 structures; 132 auxiliaries) and the frontier
section of the base PR gains the two successor rows as open targets (66 = 64 + 2), with the
two predecessor rows corrected to "conditioned on the pin V_u = H_f u = 0".

What this does not establish: nothing is proved; no inhabitant of either interface is
constructed; the successor leaves sphereMeasure a given beyond support and total area, and
does not state frame invariance or integrability; the predecessor Props and interface are
unchanged and stay registered; no claim-level label moves; alignment of every statement is
PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Stacked on the frontier docs branch; no change to check.py,
test_check.py, Specifications.lean, the lock, the toolchain or the proof packet.

Scientific effect: NONE. Organizational-independence credit 0.

